Some days I just <mark>feel down</mark>. It happens fairly often. I can never quite put my finger on why. Maybe it’s one thing, or maybe it’s a mix of things. The more I think about it, the more complicated it gets, and overthinking usually just makes me <mark>feel worse</mark>.

Today was one of those days. Maybe it was the bad dream I had last night, my <mark>messed-up sleep schedule</mark>, the usual worries, or feeling a little overwhelmed about becoming a parent next month. Still, I somehow managed to <mark>shake it off</mark>. I went to work, got a few things done for <mark>extra pay</mark>, came home, hit the gym, and now I’m planning to go out for dinner with my wife.

When I’m feeling down, going for a walk or hitting the gym is probably the simplest, cheapest, and most reliable thing I can do. But sometimes even <mark>getting started</mark> feels like too much. I need to remember not to <mark>sit around ruminating</mark> and just get out of the house.
